{"title":"Naval Architect Roadmap","role":"Naval Architect","summary":"A Naval Architect applies engineering, mathematics and marine science to the design, analysis, construction, testing and operation of ships and floating structures. The discipline covers vessel stability, hydrodynamics, structures, resistance and propulsion, ship production, safety and increasingly digital ship design.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Tech / B.E. — Naval Architecture & Ship Building"},"about":[],"intro":[{"type":"table","header":["Item","Roadmap"],"rows":[[{"text":"Starts"},{"text":"Year 1 UG · 2026"}],[{"text":"Degree"},{"text":"B.Tech / B.E."}],[{"text":"Specialisation"},{"text":"Naval Architecture & Ship Building"}],[{"text":"Target career"},{"text":"Naval Architect"}],[{"text":"Primary industries"},{"text":"Shipbuilding, ship design, defence, offshore, marine transportation, ports, classification, maritime consulting"}],[{"text":"Core domains"},{"text":"Ship design, hydrostatics, hydrodynamics, marine structures, stability, propulsion, production"}],[{"text":"Typical entry"},{"text":"Graduate Naval Architect / Junior Naval Architect / Design Engineer"}],[{"text":"Long-term roles"},{"text":"Naval Architect → Senior Naval Architect → Lead/Principal Naval Architect → Design Manager / Technical Director"}]]}],"horizons":[{"period":"2026–2030","question":"What can I enter now?","output":"Graduate Naval Architect, Ship Design Engineer, Structural Engineer, Hydrodynamics Engineer, Shipbuilding Engineer"},{"period":"2030–2035","question":"How should I specialise?","output":"Ship design, hydrodynamics, marine structures, offshore, production, defence or digital shipbuilding"},{"period":"2035–2040","question":"How should I evolve?","output":"Senior Naval Architect, Lead Designer, Principal Engineer, Project/Design Manager"},{"period":"2040–2046","question":"How can I remain relevant?","output":"Autonomous vessels, digital twins, alternative fuels, green shipping, advanced materials and computational ship design"}],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"This is a directly aligned career for a B.Tech/B.E. in Naval Architecture & Ship Building."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"These are planning horizons rather than guaranteed promotion timelines."}]},{"heading":"What to Build Each Year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["When","Build this","Learn from","Proof of progress","Gap it moves"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1 Sem 1"},{"text":"Engineering mathematics, mechanics, physics and CAD"},{"text":"College + NPTEL"},{"text":"Basic CAD ship geometry"},{"text":"Engineering foundation"}],[{"text":"Year 1 Sem 2"},{"text":"Engineering drawing, fluid mechanics and material science"},{"text":"NPTEL + labs"},{"text":"Hull-form drawing"},{"text":"Marine fundamentals"}],[{"text":"Year 2 Sem 1"},{"text":"Hydrostatics, ship geometry and stability"},{"text":"Marine labs + NPTEL"},{"text":"Hydrostatic calculation sheet"},{"text":"Ship-design capability"}],[{"text":"Year 2 Sem 2"},{"text":"Hydrodynamics, resistance and propulsion"},{"text":"CFD/NPTEL + lab"},{"text":"Resistance estimation project"},{"text":"Hydrodynamic capability"}],[{"text":"Year 3 Sem 1"},{"text":"Marine structures and structural analysis"},{"text":"FEA + structural projects"},{"text":"Hull girder/FEA analysis"},{"text":"Structural capability"}],[{"text":"Year 3 Sem 2"},{"text":"Shipbuilding, production and internship"},{"text":"Shipyard + industry exposure"},{"text":"Shipbuilding process report"},{"text":"Industry readiness"}],[{"text":"Year 4 Sem 1"},{"text":"Integrated ship design + simulation"},{"text":"Major project"},{"text":"Complete vessel design"},{"text":"Professional capability"}],[{"text":"Year 4 Sem 2"},{"text":"Internship/placement + design portfolio"},{"text":"Industry + mock interviews"},{"text":"Portfolio + technical presentation"},{"text":"Employability"}]]},{"type":"p","text":"Useful foundational learning can be built through NPTEL courses in fluid mechanics, structural engineering, CAD/CAE, CFD and related engineering subjects.","url":"https://nptel.ac.in/"},{"type":"h","text":"Core Technical Stack"},{"type":"h","text":"1. Ship Design Fundamentals"},{"type":"p","text":"Master:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Lines plan"},{"text":"Body plan"},{"text":"General arrangement"},{"text":"Ship geometry"},{"text":"Principal dimensions"},{"text":"Displacement"},{"text":"Deadweight"},{"text":"Lightweight"},{"text":"Draft"},{"text":"Freeboard"},{"text":"Block coefficient"},{"text":"Prismatic coefficient"},{"text":"Waterplane coefficient"},{"text":"Centre of buoyancy"},{"text":"Centre of gravity"},{"text":"Hydrostatic curves"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand the complete flow:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Requirements","Concept design","Hull form","Hydrostatics","Stability","Resistance","Propulsion","Structures","Systems","Production","Testing"]}]},{"heading":"Ship Stability","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"This is one of the most important technical areas."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Buoyancy"},{"text":"Equilibrium"},{"text":"Centre of gravity"},{"text":"Centre of buoyancy"},{"text":"Metacentre"},{"text":"Metacentric height"},{"text":"Righting arm"},{"text":"GZ curve"},{"text":"Intact stability"},{"text":"Damage stability"},{"text":"Free-surface effect"},{"text":"Trim"},{"text":"Heel"},{"text":"Flooding"},{"text":"Stability criteria"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Be able to calculate and interpret a vessel's stability rather than only memorising formulas."}]},{"heading":"Hydrodynamics","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Fluid mechanics"},{"text":"Ship resistance"},{"text":"Wave resistance"},{"text":"Frictional resistance"},{"text":"Form resistance"},{"text":"Propeller theory"},{"text":"Propeller-hull interaction"},{"text":"Wake"},{"text":"Cavitation"},{"text":